---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Resume"
  description="Resume of Abdurakhmon Dadaboev, an AI vision engineer with experience in road-data pipelines, segmentation, OCR, and applied machine learning."
>
  <section class="resume-header">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Resume · Updated August 2026</p>
      <h1>Abdurakhmon Dadaboev</h1>
      <p class="role">AI Vision Engineer · Data Scientist</p>
    </div>
    <div class="resume-summary">
      <p>Computer vision engineer with foundations in electronic engineering and graduate research in Big Data Science. Experienced in road-image data pipelines, segmentation, similarity search, offline OCR, and multilingual technical collaboration.</p>
      <div class="contact-row">
        <a href="mailto:dadaboev170998@gmail.com">dadaboev170998@gmail.com</a>
        <span>Sejong, South Korea</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="resume-layout">
    <div class="resume-main">
      <section class="resume-section">
        <h2>Experience</h2>

        <article class="entry">
          <div class="entry-heading"><div><h3>AI Vision Research Intern</h3><p>Youngchang Labs</p></div><time>Jul 2026</time></div>
          <ul>
            <li>Built and analyzed road-image datasets and supported computer vision model development.</li>
            <li>Developed a Mapillary-based workflow for collecting North American road imagery.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="entry">
          <div class="entry-heading"><div><h3>North American Road Data & Auto-Labeling</h3><p>Hyundai Motor Genesis Chassis Test Team · Vegas · Korea University</p></div><time>Jul 2026 — Present</time></div>
          <ul>
            <li>Designed a Mapillary API collection structure with region, capture-time, and resolution conditions.</li>
            <li>Applied DINOv3 feature vectors and FAISS similarity search to screen and organize visually similar road images.</li>
            <li>Developed a review tool that keeps human validation inside the data-curation workflow.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="entry">
          <div class="entry-heading"><div><h3>Offline Exam OCR System Developer</h3><p>Big Data Mining Lab · Korea University</p></div><time>Feb 2026 — Present</time></div>
          <ul>
            <li>Designed the system architecture and core implementation for offline exam digitization.</li>
            <li>Connected PDF alignment, OMR-based student matching, answer-region extraction, OCR, and result storage.</li>
            <li>Considered local execution, memory use, and the end-user workflow alongside recognition quality.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="entry">
          <div class="entry-heading"><div><h3>AI Vision Researcher</h3><p>Crowdsourcing-based Mobility Support · Project R2320973</p></div><time>Mar — Dec 2025</time></div>
          <ul>
            <li>Led the vision work for road-crack and pothole detection with severity classification.</li>
            <li>Demonstrated the limitations of bounding boxes for thin, irregular cracks and established a polygon-labeling standard with project partners.</li>
            <li>Reached the target performance and obtained an official model test report from AIWorks (TWR-202512-A-0072).</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="entry">
          <div class="entry-heading"><div><h3>Graduate Teaching Assistant</h3><p>Department of Big Data Science · Korea University</p></div><time>Sep 2024 — Dec 2025</time></div>
          <ul>
            <li>Supported Text Mining, Deep Learning Theory, Statistics, and Multivariate Analysis courses.</li>
            <li>Led Python and R practical sessions, prepared repositories and datasets, mentored project teams, and supported grading in Korean and English.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </section>

      <section class="resume-section">
        <h2>Research & selected work</h2>

        <article class="entry compact">
          <div class="entry-heading"><div><h3>Efficient Semantic Segmentation: Leveraging Knowledge Distillation for Modality Reduction</h3><p>AEECA 2025 · Dalian, China</p></div><time>Aug 2025</time></div>
          <p>Transferred knowledge from a multi-modal RGB, NIR, and LiDAR teacher to an RGB-only student model to reduce sensor requirements.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="entry compact">
          <div class="entry-heading"><div><h3>AI Hub Image Data Education Framework</h3><p>Eco-Up Innovation Fusion University · Project R2320813</p></div><time>Sep 2024 — Jan 2025</time></div>
          <p>Analyzed six AI Hub data fields and created a unified Python framework for image-data exploration, preprocessing, and modeling.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="entry compact">
          <div class="entry-heading"><div><h3>Embedded Systems Projects</h3><p>Sun Moon University</p></div><time>2021 — 2022</time></div>
          <p>Built an Arduino hexapod robot and a Raspberry Pi vision-guided ball launcher, combining sensors, motor control, circuit design, and OpenCV.</p>
        </article>
      </section>
    </div>

    <aside class="resume-aside">
      <section>
        <h2>Education</h2>
        <div class="aside-item"><h3>M.S. Big Data Science</h3><p>Korea University, Sejong</p><span>2024 — Aug 2026 expected</span><strong>GPA 4.46 / 4.5</strong></div>
        <div class="aside-item"><h3>B.S. Electronic Engineering</h3><p>Sun Moon University</p><span>2019 — 2023</span><strong>GPA 4.18 / 4.5</strong></div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Technical focus</h2>
        <div class="skill-group"><h3>Vision</h3><p>Segmentation, classification, retrieval, knowledge distillation, OCR, OMR</p></div>
        <div class="skill-group"><h3>Tools</h3><p>Python, PyTorch, OpenCV, Ultralytics YOLO, DINOv3, FAISS, SQLite, Git, Jupyter</p></div>
        <div class="skill-group"><h3>Systems</h3><p>Data curation, API pipelines, offline inference, evaluation, human review tools</p></div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Languages</h2>
        <ul class="plain-list">
          <li><strong>Uzbek</strong><span>Native</span></li>
          <li><strong>Korean</strong><span>TOPIK Level 6 · Oct 2025</span></li>
          <li><strong>English</strong><span>TOEIC 800 · Jul 2026<br />IELTS 6.5 · Speaking 7.5</span></li>
          <li><strong>Russian</strong><span>Advanced</span></li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Certificates & awards</h2>
        <ul class="plain-list">
          <li><strong>Judicial Interpreter</strong><span>2024</span></li>
          <li><strong>KIIP Stage 5</strong><span>2023</span></li>
          <li><strong>GKS Outstanding Self-Funded Student</strong><span>2020 · 2021</span></li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Leadership</h2>
        <p class="aside-copy">Led the Sun Moon University Uzbek Student Association, supported international students, built a KakaoTalk FAQ bot, and interpreted for university delegations.</p>
      </section>
    </aside>
  </div>

  <style>
    .resume-header { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(18rem, 1fr); gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem); align-items: end; padding-block: 0 2rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
    .resume-header h1 { font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 5vw, 3rem); }
    .role { margin-top: 0.7rem; color: var(--accent); font-weight: 650; }
    .resume-summary > p { font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.75; }
    .contact-row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem 1.2rem; margin-top: 1.1rem; color: var(--ink-muted); font-size: 0.88rem; }
    .contact-row a { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }
    .resume-layout { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.65fr) minmax(16rem, 0.75fr); gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem); padding-top: 2.2rem; }
    .resume-main, .resume-aside { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem; }
    .resume-section, .resume-aside section { padding: clamp(1.35rem, 3vw, 1.8rem); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius-md); background: var(--surface); }
    .resume-section > h2, .resume-aside section > h2 { margin-bottom: 1.3rem; font-size: 1rem; letter-spacing: 0.04em; text-transform: uppercase; }
    .entry { padding-block: 0 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
    .entry:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
    .entry-heading { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: start; gap: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.8rem; }
    .entry-heading h3 { margin-bottom: 0.2rem; font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.4; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
    .entry-heading p { font-size: 0.9rem; }
    time { flex: none; color: var(--ink-muted); font-size: 0.8rem; }
    .entry ul { padding-left: 1.1rem; }
    .entry li, .entry > p { margin-bottom: 0.45rem; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 0.96rem; line-height: 1.72; }
    .entry.compact { padding-bottom: 1.1rem; margin-bottom: 1.1rem; }
    .resume-aside { padding-left: 0; }
    .aside-item { margin-bottom: 1.2rem; }
    .aside-item h3, .skill-group h3 { margin-bottom: 0.2rem; font-size: 1rem; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
    .aside-item p, .aside-item span, .skill-group p, .aside-copy { display: block; font-size: 0.88rem; }
    .aside-item strong { display: block; margin-top: 0.25rem; color: var(--accent); font-size: 0.86rem; }
    .skill-group { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
    .plain-list { list-style: none; }
    .plain-list li { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; padding-block: 0.65rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); font-size: 0.86rem; }
    .plain-list strong { color: var(--ink); }
    .plain-list span { color: var(--ink-muted); text-align: right; }
    @media (max-width: 820px) { .resume-header, .resume-layout { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .resume-aside { padding-left: 0; border-left: 0; } }
    @media (max-width: 560px) { .entry-heading { flex-direction: column; gap: 0.35rem; } .plain-list li { flex-direction: column; gap: 0.15rem; } .plain-list span { text-align: left; } }
  </style>
</Layout>
